    "message": "fix(55.11-e2e B4): don't fire a second navigation after equipment submit; let the form route unmount\n\nThe equipment journey called appRouter.go(AppRoutes.equipmentCheck) right\nafter submit, on top of the form's own success navigation (_handleClose ->\ncontext.go). The two raced; the popped CustomTransitionPage (opaque:false,\ntransparent barrierColor) could leave its modal scope mounted over the\nhistory screen, and the journey's formGone widget poll reported 'gone'\nbefore the route's barrier was torn down. Mirror the green daily-log\njourney step 10 instead: poll for the form to leave the tree, then let the\nexit animation settle with bounded pumps \u2014 no second go().\n\nVerified locally on Pixel_6a (swiftshader): equipment journey green, zero\nhit-test warnings; attendance journey green with the ensureVisible fix.\n\nCorrects the diagnosis trail: this is NOT the ForUI toast \u2014 a local run\nwith the toast pinned to bottomCenter reproduced the identical top-of-screen\nabsorbing chain at (340, 209). The toast bottomCenter pin is kept\nseparately (real UX defect: a top toast covers the top filter button), but\nit is not what fixes this.",
    "timestamp": "2026-10-02T11:54:23Z",
